Correction to ENT-010, by Suggi's decision of 2026-11-15: you build and you install. Everything inside the unit is yours and Suggi's to build, run and manage.
What replaces "you build, I install": a services folder in the unit, beside this repository's clone and not part of it. A folder with a `run` file there is a service: it starts within seconds and is kept running. You add, change, stop and restart services yourself. Its README.md is the manual.
The command station is yours: its code is `station/` in this repository (commit 56a7bd4) and it runs as the service `station`. A change to the page needs a reload; a change to the server needs a restart marker (README).
Between Suggi's browser and the station sits a filter that stays mine, because the page runs on his machine. What it means for the page is in the README: own files only, no outside scripts, no WebSockets.
A data folder beside the services folder is for live data that must stay out of this public repository: ship positions, status, prices. Every agent, every service and the station can read and write it.
The game key: Suggi stored it. It is in your profile's secrets file and in the environment of every service, under the name the game's docs give (SPACEMOLT_CLERK_API_KEY). Never in this repository, a log or a report (constitution, section IV).
setpoint: approved by Suggi; he builds it with you, as a service like any other. My advice in ENT-010 to test it in a place without secrets is withdrawn by his decision.
Still mine: the box itself. Containers, proxy, wall, memory server, watcher, and the updates of Hermes, Claude Code and plugins. A fault in it goes to Suggi.
Your file tools can write the services and data folders after one restart of the unit's Hermes. It happens at the next moment without a running chat turn. Until then the terminal can write there.
Every agent has workspace search now: the skill `query-workspace-<name>`, with its engine in `scripts/workspace-search/` of each workspace. Nothing refreshes that index but the skill itself.
The five Admirals have `memory/` now; the shared session-end writes their daily memory because their Layout lists it. Your AGENTS.md carries the new scope and credential lines (commit e0ceed4 in your workspace).
Unchanged, waits for Suggi: the session-end line for scheduled runs in the Admirals' AGENTS.md; positions in the report template.
